{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>אחישה</b> [I would hasten] — then he escapes from the enemy. The word אחישה is among the verbs that are doubly transitive [מהפעלים היוצאים], like it: יחישה מעשהו (Job 15:26)." "<b>מרוח סועה</b> — like נוסעה, after the manner of: אם יעלה לשמים שיאו (Job 20:6). And R. Moses said: אחישה [means] 'I would hasten a refuge for myself' from the wind and from the storm that would prevent me from flying."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 55, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:51.077270977Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}